@startuml CycleFar Future Replanning Sequence
title CycleFar — Change future training

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Rider
boundary "Owner-scoped\nchange controller" as Controller
control "Planning change service" as ChangeService
control "FuturePrescriber" as Prescriber
control "ExistingPlanConfiguration" as ExistingConfiguration
control "PlanBuilder" as Builder
control "HorizonMaterializer" as Materializer
database "PostgreSQL" as Database

note over ChangeService
  Entry service is AvailabilityChanger, TimeOffPlanner or
  MissedWorkoutResolver, according to the rider's action.
end note

Rider -> Controller: submit change to an owned plan/workout
alt change availability
  Controller -> ChangeService: AvailabilityChanger.apply!
  ChangeService -> Database: lock plan; version availability template
  ChangeService -> ChangeService: choose one week or from-date range
else add or remove time off
  Controller -> ChangeService: TimeOffPlanner.add! / remove!
  ChangeService -> Database: lock plan; save or remove time-off period
  ChangeService -> ChangeService: group future dates by effective template
else replan after a missed workout
  Controller -> ChangeService: MissedWorkoutResolver.resolve!(replan)
  ChangeService -> Database: lock plan; retain source as missed
  ChangeService -> ChangeService: choose today through day 13 and today's template
end

loop each affected range and its selected availability slots
  ChangeService -> Prescriber: replace!(dates, slots)
  Prescriber -> Database: lock plan; read future planned workouts
  Prescriber -> Database: remove affected replaceable planned workouts
  Prescriber -> ExistingConfiguration: build from saved plan and slots
  ExistingConfiguration --> Prescriber: existing-plan configuration
  Prescriber -> Builder: preview(configuration)
  Builder --> Prescriber: deterministic prescriptions and forecasts
  Prescriber -> Prescriber: apply time-off and return-ramp rules
  Prescriber -> Database: create replacement outlines and forecasts
  Prescriber -> Materializer: call(plan)
  Materializer -> Database: lock plan; read eligible outlines
  Materializer -> Database: save canonical steps and current-FTP metrics
end
ChangeService --> Controller: change applied
Controller --> Rider: redirect to calendar

note over Prescriber, Database
  Only future planned records in the affected dates are replaceable.
  Completed and missed workouts, plan phases and event date remain.
  Missed leave/move actions do not enter this re-prescription flow.
end note
@enduml
